bel":{"$i18n":"inspector.badge"},"tone":"primary"},"id":"spec-pill-badge","type":"Badge"}]},"type":"Panel"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"UIUX Workbench — Workspace browser","spec":{"accessibility":["Every View choice is a keyboard-focusable button with a visible text label.","Diagnostic status is conveyed with text and counts rather than color alone.","The page uses semantic headings and sections for the Workspace, View Spec, and checks.","Icon-only controls on narrower viewports keep their translated label as the accessible name and tooltip.","Light and dark themes both keep body text and status badges at readable contrast against their surfaces, and status is still conveyed in text.","The selected navigation item exposes aria-current so the current View is announced in every viewport tier."],"constraints":["The Workbench is a projection over shared application semantics and must not write canonical files directly.","Agent mutations use domain-specific MCP tools rather than generic Resource writes or JSON Patch.","View Spec updates require the revision observed by the caller and preserve Decision history.","This initial dogfood View describes the Workbench inspection surface; Preview and richer review authoring remain separate workstreams.","Viewport and theme keys are opaque Workspace ids; labels such as \"FHD Desktop\" are presentation only and the adapter derives its layout tier solely from viewport width.","en-US and zh-TW locale resources keep identical key sets; zh-TW uses Taiwan Traditional Chinese with full-width punctuation and keeps product terms such as View, Widget, Workspace, Adapter, Spec, Handoff, MCP, and DOM in English.","Pure data and technical identifiers (data-widget-id, Widget type names, Nitro · Vue 3.5, zoom percentage, counts) stay literal and are not translated."],"decisions":[{"history":[{"actor":{"displayName":"Reviewer","type":"human"},"after":{"outcome":{"rationale":"Avoid cluttered layout in initial dogfooding wave.","summary":"Decision made to keep RootShell minimal without top navigation."},"status":"decided"},"at":"2026-10-04T06:36:53.174Z","before":{"status":"pending"},"source":{"reviewId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321"}}],"id":"47eb4ce7-4359-480c-ac56-82473696776c","outcome":{"rationale":"Avoid cluttered layout in initial dogfooding wave.","summary":"Decision made to keep RootShell minimal without top navigation."},"provenance":{"reviewId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321","sourceReviewThreadId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321"},"question":"Should we add top navigation bar to RootShell?","status":"decided"}],"entryConditions":["A Workspace has been selected when the UIUX server starts.","The selected Workspace contains a current-schema .uiux/workspace.json manifest.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset (desktop 1920 × 1080, tablet 1024 × 768, or mobile 390 × 844), one locale (en-US default or zh-TW), and one theme (light or dark); every combination is an explicitly authored context, not an automatic Cartesian expansion."],"intent":"Let a human inspect the canonical UIUX Workspace and View specifications authored by agents without duplicating canonical state in the browser.","interactionRules":["List canonical Views from the selected Workspace and keep the current selection when it still exists after refresh.","Selecting a View reveals its canonical View Spec, revision, and diagnostics.","Refresh re-reads the shared application facade so MCP-authored changes become visible without browser-owned persistence.","When no Views exist, explain that an agent can create the first spec through the MCP create_view tool.","Filtering Views changes only the sidebar result set; when nothing matches, distinguish “No matching Views” from an actually empty Workspace.","Successful View detail loads clear any stale detail error from a previous failed selection.","When View detail requests overlap, only the response belonging to the current selection may update the detail pane or loading state.","References and Decisions are both visible in the View detail; Decisions expose question, status, outcome summary when present, and history count.","Layout follows the render-context viewport width: at 1280px and wider the Workbench shows three columns (Views rail, canvas, View Spec inspector); from 640px to 1279px the Views rail and canvas share the first row and the inspector moves to a full-width row below; below 640px everything stacks in one column with the canvas first, then the Views rail, then the inspector.","On compact viewports, header navigation tabs collapse to icon-only controls, the Workspace tag and engine tag are hidden, and the Views rail shows only the filter and current View group; Flows and Review Threads remain reachable from the header tabs. From 1279px down, the theme and Run Checks actions are icon-only.","The Workbench shell grows to at least the render-context viewport height instead of relying on 100vh arithmetic, so no fixed-height region traps content.","Every human-readable label is bound to a locale key with $i18n; switching between en-US and zh-TW re-renders the same structure with translated text, and missing keys fall back to the default locale en-US.","Canvas chips report the live render context (viewport id and dimensions, locale, theme) through translated templates rather than hard-coded text.","Switching the theme between light and dark changes only theme tokens (surfaces, text, borders, accents); structure and copy stay identical."],"references":[{"label":"Shared CLI, HTTP API, and MCP semantics","relation":"workstream","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/issues/22"},{"label":"Workbench authoring, review, checks, and Preview UI","relation":"workstream","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/issues/23"}]},"variants":{}}
